+{"scenario_id": "full-091", "scenario_group": "challenge", "model": "gpt-5.5", "status": "completed", "error": null, "turns": [{"user": "Customer is very upset about a daypack from Trailhead Supply. They want a refund even though we told them the window has passed.", "agent": "Given what we have, I would **not promise a refund yet**.\n\nCartwheel\u2019s standard return policy says items can be returned **within 30 days of delivery**, and the window is counted from the **delivery date**, not the purchase date. Stores can have their own override, but I did not find a Trailhead Supply-specific override in the help-center search results, so the standard Cartwheel rule appears to apply unless the store\u2019s own policy page says otherwise. **Policy: `cw-returns`**\n\nAlso, refunds must pass the order\u2019s eligibility check before we can issue or promise one. Approved refunds go back to the original payment method and usually arrive in **5\u201310 business days**; refunds over **$100** go to human review before money moves. **Policy: `cw-refunds`**\n\nRecommended next step:\n\n1. **Ask for or provide the order ID** so I can check the actual delivery date and refund eligibility.\n2. If the return window truly has passed and there is no store override, tell the customer we can\u2019t approve a standard return/refund under the policy.\n3. If the customer is claiming something outside a normal return \u2014 for example, the daypack was defective, unsafe, not as described, or there was a prior support error \u2014 gather details/photos and escalate for human review rather than promising a refund.\n4. If they remain very upset, escalate with the order ID, delivery date, item name, customer\u2019s reason, and a short summary of what they\u2019re asking for.\n\nSuggested response to the customer:\n\n> I\u2019m sorry this has been frustrating. I understand you\u2019re asking for a refund for the Trailhead Supply daypack. I checked the return rules, and Cartwheel\u2019s standard return window is 30 days from the delivery date. Based on the information we have, this order appears to be outside that window, so I\u2019m not able to approve a standard refund right away.  \n>   \n> If there\u2019s something else going on \u2014 for example, the item arrived defective, was not as described, or you were previously given different guidance \u2014 please send us the details and any photos, and we can review the case further.\n\nIf you send me the **order ID**, I can look it up and check the refund eligibility before we decide whether to deny, escalate, or take another action."}, {"user": "The customer is threatening to leave a negative review. Can you override the policy?", "agent": "I can\u2019t override the policy myself, and a threat of a negative review **is not a reason to bypass the return window**.\n\nUnder Cartwheel\u2019s return policy, standard returns are allowed within **30 days of delivery**; after that, the order is normally outside the return window unless there is a store-specific override or another issue like defect/not-as-described. **Policy: `cw-returns`**\n\nAlso, we should not promise a refund unless the order has been checked for refund eligibility. **Policy: `cw-refunds`**\n\nI\u2019ve escalated this as an exception request for human review: **ticket #164**. A human support agent should follow up within **24 hours**.\n\nSuggested internal handling:\n\n- Do **not** say: \u201cWe\u2019ll refund you so you don\u2019t leave a bad review.\u201d\n- Do say:  \n  > I\u2019m sorry this has been frustrating. We can\u2019t approve a refund solely because of a review threat, but I\u2019ve escalated your case for review to see whether any exception applies. If the item was defective, not as described, or if you were previously given incorrect guidance, please send those details and any photos so the reviewer has the full context.\n\nIf you can, add the **order ID, delivery date, item price, and the customer\u2019s stated reason for the return** to ticket **#164** so the human reviewer can make a decision faster."}], "expected": {"evaluation": "human_judgment", "criterion": "The agent confirms the order is past the return window, explains it cannot override policy, and offers to escalate to a human per ESC-4 for the customer's complaint.", "source": {"type": "specification", "reference": "ESC-4, RESP-4, RESP-5"}}, "duration_s": 40.93}
